                    {
                        "translation_id": "6662443c-355b-4db2-873a-72c3f6c8300c",
                        "source_entry_id": "53944507-0505-354f-9f31-41293deb6f88",
                        "source_sense_id": "0d76f2a0-266f-3dee-bf88-b6990c7523a4",
                        "target_lang_word": "jinriksha",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "jinriksha",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7c8361dc-15cf-3347-aa12-289445848790",
                                        "entry_id": "bbc9be75-9e6d-3511-bd67-dda199333ac2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of rickshaw."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46d47885-a00d-478c-a81d-faf700ded89b",
                                                "sense_id": "7c8361dc-15cf-3347-aa12-289445848790",
                                                "text": "There are no roads outside the villages in northern Yezo, no jinriksha,—those most fascinating man-power carriages,—no kago, or swinging cars, and no side-saddles..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d12d9812-f890-4031-8eb9-a50bf2973127",
                                                "sense_id": "7c8361dc-15cf-3347-aa12-289445848790",
                                                "text": "In the Transportation Buildin' is a map one hundred feet long, showing the transportation facilities of the Empire, a perfect network of railways and telegraphand telephone wires, showin' they have other ways of gettin' 'round there besides man-carts and jinrikshas, yes, indeed!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "242ab5b3-8de7-4222-b0fe-f1a67cb725b8",
                                                "sense_id": "7c8361dc-15cf-3347-aa12-289445848790",
                                                "text": "Then a treat is in store for me! Three jinriksha are procured, and we ride off to the station. My, what a thrill!!!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d5f6f1d7-d21a-49a7-b1cc-f1d92b020404",
                        "source_entry_id": "53944507-0505-354f-9f31-41293deb6f88",
                        "source_sense_id": "0d76f2a0-266f-3dee-bf88-b6990c7523a4",
                        "target_lang_word": "jinrikisha",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "jinrikisha",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dc0778a4-fce7-3e5c-b7a1-f5f1d21c21cf",
                                        "entry_id": "a22893d8-ae76-31bc-a3cd-5a56ae551d5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of jinriksha."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95b291d8-d128-4acd-aa2f-906322a91e3b",
                                                "sense_id": "dc0778a4-fce7-3e5c-b7a1-f5f1d21c21cf",
                                                "text": "So we take our way in two jinrikisha to the Temple Rin-ko-ji, on Kuboyama. We roll swiftly through a mile of many-colored narrow Japanese streets; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81c2c3f5-76fe-4ff7-b963-91f1da878f8b",
                                                "sense_id": "dc0778a4-fce7-3e5c-b7a1-f5f1d21c21cf",
                                                "text": "Of course the first thing that struck us were the queer wheelbarrows used by the native population in place of the jinrikishas adopted from Japan for the Europeans."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
